# Rust coding

Read `.cursor/skills/rust-fundamentals/SKILL.md` when writing non-trivial Rust.

## Always

- `Result`/`Option`; map errors at boundaries
- `cargo fmt`; Clippy with warnings denied in CI mindset
- Feature-gate Tokio; avoid `full` by default
- Document `unsafe` with `// SAFETY:`

## Never

- `unwrap`/`expect` in production paths
- Hold `std::sync::Mutex` across `.await`
- Ignore spawned task `JoinHandle` results
- `println!` instead of `tracing` in libraries

## Prefer

- Owned data at async boundaries
- `thiserror` for library/domain errors
- Small `pub` surfaces (`pub(crate)` default)
